{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And it shall be a fading flower.</b> As if he said: this flower that shall fade, like <i>daughter of Babylon, the devastated</i> (Psalms 137:8), or <b>flower of a fading leaf</b>, and this is the correct reading." "<b>Like the first-ripe.</b> It is the first fig, ripening before the summer fruit comes."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:29.503604371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}